## 2. Managing Version Locks Across Multiple Tabs (`versionchange`)

A common bug occurs when **Tab A** opens a new version of the site requiring a database schema upgrade while **Tab B** is still open with an older database connection active.

IndexedDB handles this using the **`onversionchange`** and **`onblocked`** events.

```text
┌─────────────────┐       Open DB v2 (Requires Schema Change) ┌──────────────────┐
│ Tab A           │ ─────────────────────────────────────────► │ IndexedDB Engine │
└─────────────────┘                                            └────────┬─────────┘
                                                                        │
                                   Triggers 'versionchange' Event       │
                                ◄───────────────────────────────────────┤
                                                                        │
┌─────────────────┐       (Tab B must close connection)                │
│ Tab B (Open DB) │ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
└─────────────────┘

```

### Complete Cross-Tab Upgrade Handler

```javascript
// Function to connect to IndexedDB with robust cross-tab lifecycle management
function connectWithVersionHandling(targetVersion) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const request = indexedDB.open("AppDatabase", targetVersion);

    // 1. Triggered when this tab requests a database schema upgrade
    request.onupgradeneeded = (event) => {
      console.log("Upgrading database schema...");
      const db = event.target.result;
      if (!db.objectStoreNames.contains("settings")) {
        db.createObjectStore("settings", { keyPath: "key" });
      }
    };

    // 2. Triggered if OTHER tabs refuse to close their connection, blocking this upgrade
    request.onblocked = () => {
      alert("Please close other open tabs of this app to update to the latest version!");
    };

    request.onsuccess = (event) => {
      const db = event.target.result;

      // 3. Listen for OTHER tabs attempting to perform a schema upgrade
      db.onversionchange = () => {
        // Close connection immediately so the other tab isn't blocked from upgrading
        db.close();
        alert("A new version of this app was loaded in another tab. Reloading page...");
        window.location.reload();
      };

      resolve(db);
    };

    request.onerror = () => reject(request.error);
  });
}

```

