## 3. Real-Time Cross-Tab UI Synchronization

IndexedDB does **not** natively emit events when data inside a table changes. If **Tab A** inserts a record into IndexedDB, **Tab B** won't know about it automatically.

To sync IndexedDB mutations across tabs, combine IndexedDB with the **`BroadcastChannel` API**.

```javascript
// db-sync.js - Cross-Tab IndexedDB Synchronizer
const syncChannel = new BroadcastChannel("idb_sync_channel");

class SyncedDB {
  constructor() {
    this.db = null;
  }

  async init() {
    this.db = await openDB();

    // Listen for mutations performed by other tabs
    syncChannel.onmessage = (event) => {
      const { type, storeName, key } = event.data;
      console.log(`[Cross-Tab Sync] Event ${type} on store "${storeName}" at key:`, key);

      // Trigger UI update in this tab
      this.onExternalChange(storeName, key);
    };
  }

  // Mutate data and notify other tabs
  async updateUserBalance(userId, newBalance) {
    const tx = this.db.transaction("users", "readwrite");
    const store = tx.objectStore("users");

    await store.put({ id: userId, balance: newBalance });

    tx.oncomplete = () => {
      // Broadcast mutation event to all OTHER tabs
      syncChannel.postMessage({
        type: "MUTATION_PUT",
        storeName: "users",
        key: userId,
        timestamp: Date.now()
      });
    };
  }

  // Handle external updates arriving from BroadcastChannel
  async onExternalChange(storeName, key) {
    if (storeName === "users") {
      const tx = this.db.transaction("users", "readonly");
      const user = await tx.objectStore("users").get(key);
      
      // Re-render local UI with fresh database value
      console.log("Updating local UI with newly synced user data:", user);
    }
  }
}

// Usage in Page
const appDB = new SyncedDB();
appDB.init();

```

