## Key Design Patterns & Tradeoffs

| Challenge                 | Strategy                          | Solution                                                                                                                        |
| ------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Instant UI Updates**    | **Optimistic UI**                 | Write immediately to IndexedDB with a temporary client-generated key before network requests complete.                          |
| **Unreliable Networks**   | **Outbox Queue Pattern**          | Decouple UI saves from API calls by storing mutation payloads in a `sync-outbox` queue.                                         |
| **Conflict Resolution**   | **Server Wins / Last Write Wins** | Overwrite local temporary records with server-validated payloads once the network sync completes.                               |
| **Browser Compatibility** | **Sync Fallback**                 | Fall back to listening for `window.addEventListener('online')` on browsers lacking native `SyncManager` support (e.g., Safari). |
